{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118545","id":3525399686,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7SIVSG","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118545","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118545.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118545.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118545","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118545/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118545/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118545/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2efcd05d7eb79a98b8d5ad6f8f61581942736edc","number":118545,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Prevent re-entrant Main::iteration() in ProgressDialog::_update_ui","user":{"login":"dsarno","id":2432103,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzIxMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2432103?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno","html_url":"https://github.com/dsarno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsarno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #118544\r\n\r\n**Note to maintainers:** This is not an AI slop PR..  I'm the lead maintainer on the 8,000 star Unity-MCP project. I do use LLMs to build (like many engineers), but I also make sure changes are minimal, follow project culture, and are well tested. I rebuilt Godot with the fix and tested it thoroughly. Just thought I'd let you know.  At unity-mcp, we get a ton of slop too, so anyway, hello from a real human!\r\n\r\n## What happens\r\n\r\n`ProgressDialog::_update_ui()` calls `Main::iteration()` with no re-entrancy guard. This runs a full frame cycle including `_process()` on all `@tool` nodes. If any plugin's `_process()` triggers a save (directly or indirectly), the call chain recurses: `_save_scene_with_preview` → `EditorProgress::step()` → `_update_ui()` → `Main::iteration()` → `_process()` → `save_scene()` → ... The stack overflows after ~1000 frames and the editor crashes (SIGSEGV).\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nAdds a static `is_iterating` guard to `_update_ui()` — if `Main::iteration()` is already running from a prior `_update_ui()` call up the stack, the nested call is skipped. Same pattern as `prevent_recursive_process_hack` in `EditorFileSystem` (#73214 / #54864).\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- [ ] Enable the MRP plugin from #118544 (a `@tool` plugin that calls `EditorInterface.save_scene()` from `_process()`)\r\n- [ ] Without fix: editor crashes within seconds (SIGSEGV, stack overflow from 1000+ recursive `_process()` frames)\r\n- [ ] With fix: editor stays alive, no recursion — `_update_ui()` returns early on re-entrant calls\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=",